    <item>
      <title>Election Interference Is Hard. Messing With Your Mind Is Easy</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-20/election-interference-is-hard-messing-with-your-mind-is-easy</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">cef61a5b69239b47f7dbbd6f</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:00:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>You’ve likely heard the ominous what-if scenarios about election disruptions in November: immigration agents or federal troops roaming polling places, federal officials seizing ballots and voting machines, and President Donald Trump issuing an executive order postponing or cancelling the election. Courts and legal experts have given solid reasons that each one of those potential election disruptions is unlikely. But the threats have served their purpose: People are harboring doubts.</description>
      <dc:creator>Mary Ellen Klas</dc:creator>
